====================================================================================================
(4) FIRST-ORDER FIELD g_tot AND THE SHARP CONSTANT
====================================================================================================
g_tot: phi = x + s g_tot + O(s^2);  g_tot = 0 on (-a,0), -x^2/L on (0,L), free on I'.
Q[g] := (1/(48 pi^2)) int_0^inf k^3 |ghat(k)|^2 dk = lim_{s->0} E(s)/s^2 .
Minimised over the extension (linear least squares, basis size M):
     M      Q_min          9*Q_min (=Q of the zeta-normalised field)   4.5*Q_min
     30     0.00188117     0.01693049                                 0.00846525
     60     0.00187958     0.01691624                                 0.00845812
     90     0.00187894     0.01691049                                 0.00845525
     140    0.00187792     0.01690128                                 0.00845064
     200    0.00187764     0.01689879                                 0.00844939
     unoptimised (cubic-Hermite) extension:  Q = 0.00248322,  4.5*Q = 0.01117448

     g_B/4 = 1/(6 pi^2)  = 0.01688686   <-> 9*Q_min  (the zeta-normalised first-order field)
     g_B/8 = 1/(12 pi^2) = 0.00844343   <-> 4.5*Q_min = lim_{zeta->0} (1/2)E/zeta^2
     Richardson (1/M) extrapolation from M=140,200:  Q_inf = 0.00187700, 9*Q_inf = 0.01689298,  4.5*Q_inf = 0.00844649  (g_B/8 = 0.00844343)

  RESTRICTED class: extensions with u -> 0 at |x| = infinity, i.e. gt(pi)=gt'(pi)=0
  (the circle field must vanish to second order at the point at infinity):
     M=30   Q_min = 0.01522146   4.5*Q_min = 0.06849657   ratio to g_B/8 = 8.112
     M=60   Q_min = 0.01512450   4.5*Q_min = 0.06806027   ratio to g_B/8 = 8.061
     M=90   Q_min = 0.01506655   4.5*Q_min = 0.06779949   ratio to g_B/8 = 8.030

  CONCLUSION: inf over extensions of (1/2)E/zeta^2 -> g_B/8 = 1/(12 pi^2) to ~0.1%,
  Phi <= (1/2)E holds for every extension tested, and (1/2)E/Phi -> 1 from above as zeta -> 0.
